meta {
  name: VTON 2D Internal Proxy
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/vton/2d
  body: multipartForm
  auth: none
}

headers {
  X-Manikan-Key: {{apiKey}}
  X-Request-Id: req_test_001
}

body:multipart-form {
  human_image: @file(/path/to/person_photo.jpg)
  product_id: {{productId}}
  session_id: sess_abc123xyz789
}

docs {
  ## POST /api/vton/2d

  **Internal Service Proxy.** This endpoint is the protected hop between
  the widget gateway (`/api/widget/vton`) and the Python VTON service.

  > ⚠️ **NOT intended for direct browser/shopper calls.**
  > The sole storefront entrypoint is `/api/vton/2d/proxy` or `/api/widget/vton`.
  > This endpoint is gated by a **service-level key** (`VTON_2D` service key),
  > not a widget public key.

  ### Authentication
  `X-Manikan-Key` must contain a service-level API key checked by `authorizeServiceRequest`.

  ### Form Fields
  | Field       | Type   | Required | Description                                   |
  |-------------|--------|----------|-----------------------------------------------|
  | human_image | File   | ✅       | Person photo (image/*, max 5MB)               |
  | product_id  | string | ✅       | Product ID — garment image fetched from DB    |
  | session_id  | string | ❌       | Optional session ID for caching/tracking      |

  ### SSRF Prevention
  The garment image URL is fetched from the database (not client-supplied).
  The URL is validated against an `VTON_ALLOWED_IMAGE_HOSTS` allowlist to
  prevent the Python service being used as an SSRF primitive.

  ### Category Aliases
  Product categories are normalized: `"tops"` → `"shirt"`, `"trousers"` → `"pants"`, etc.
  Unsupported categories return `422 UNSUPPORTED_CATEGORY`.

  ### Timeout
  150 seconds (VTON may take up to 120s for diffusion model inference + polling).

  ### Success (200)
  Returns the try-on image binary with appropriate `Content-Type`.
}
